          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#Definition In point-set topology
          %p
            The following is the classical discussion of universal covering spaces in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
          #SimplyConnectedCoveringUniqueness.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+unique"} essential uniqueness
                of simply connected covering spaces)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"}> path-connected
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+path-connected+topological+space"}> locally path connected
                  \.
            %p
              Then if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_i \overset{p_i}{\to} X
              are two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \{1,2\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"} path-connected
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              as covering spaces.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
              are simply connected, the assumption of the lifting theorem for covering spaces is satisfied (
              %a{:href => "covering+space#TheTheoremLifting"}> this prop.
              ). This says that there are horizontal continuous function making the following diagrams commute:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAAA
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E_1 &amp;&amp; \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; E_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{p_1}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_2}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
                    \\phantom{AAAAAA}
                    \\array{
                    E_2 &amp;&amp; \overset{g}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; E_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{p_2}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_1}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi i
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E_i &amp;&amp; \overset{id}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; E_i
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{p_i}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_i}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              and that these are
              %em unique
              once we specify the image of a single point, which we may freely do (in the given fiber).
            %p
              So if we pick any point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat x_1 \in E_1
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\hat x) = x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat x_2 \in E_2
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\hat x_2) = x
              and specify that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\hat x_1) = \hat x_2
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(\hat x_2) = \hat x_1
              then uniqueness applied to the composites implies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g = id_{E_{2}}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f = id_{E_1}
          #CoveringUniversal.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (universal covering space)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"}> path-connected
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+path-connected+topological+space"}> locally path connected
                  \.
            %p
              Then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"} path-connected
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %em universal covering space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplyConnectedCoveringUniqueness"}
          #ReconstructCoveringForFreeAndTransitiveMonodromyRepresentation.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
                reconstructed from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a topological space which is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-connected+space"} well-connected
              in that it is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+space"}> path-connected
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+path-connected+space"} locally path-connected
              %li
                %p
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-locally+simply-connected+space"} semi-locally simply-connected
            %p
              Then a universal covering space of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringUniversal"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "covering+space#CoveringConnectivityViaMonodromy"} this prop.
              the covering space is connected and simply connected precisely if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
              representation is free and transitive. By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              arises as the monodromy of some covering space. Hence it remains to see that a free and transitive representation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              exists. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              be any point, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(x,-)
              is such a representation.
          %p This is a functorial construction of a universal covering spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mo *
                    %mi wc
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Cov
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Top_*^{wc} \longrightarrow Cov_*
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mo *
                    %mi wc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_*^{wc}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_*
            on the well-connected spaces and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cov
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cov
            is the subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mo *
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_*^2
            of pointed maps of spaces with objects the covering space maps.
          %p
            Specifically, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a space with basepoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}
            to be the space whose points are homotopy classes of paths in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            starting at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}\to X
            projecting to the endpoint of a path. We can equip this set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}\to X
            with a topology coming from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            so that it becomes a universal covering space as above. As described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            = succeed "-actions," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}
            corresponds to the “regular representation” of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+representation"} regular representation
              can be seen to arise by taking a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
              in the same way that the regular representation of a group is gotten by taking its action on itself: we can see that the
              %em universal covering groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)^{(1)}
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Grpd}/\Pi(X)
              (see the universal covering
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
              on itself, and can be topologized in a natural way by lifting the topology on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              along the canonical projection
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)^{(1)} \to \Pi(X)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}
          %h3#InCohesiveHomotopyTheory In cohesive homotopy theory
          %p
            We describe now how the universal cover construction may be understood from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fragment"} fragment
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+theory"} cohesive homotopy theory
          %p
            The basic idea is that the universal cover of a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of the canonical morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \longrightarrow \Pi_1(X)
          %p
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} topological ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
            to become trivial in a universal way”.
          #ExamplesOfCohesiveToposesOfTopologicalGroupoids.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong (cohesive higher toposes of topological groupoids)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              be some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-cohesive+site"} ∞-cohesive site
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
              and consider
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H} \coloneqq Sh_\infty(\mathcal{S})
            %p
              the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              over this site. This is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"}> topological ∞-groupoids
              ” modeled on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            %p
              A canonical choice relating to the traditional discussion would be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi lcont
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S} = Top^\kappa_{lcont}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+contractible+topological+spaces"} locally contractible topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              might be called “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+contractible+topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"}> locally contractible topological ∞-groupoids
              ”.
            %p
              A more restrictive choice would be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S} =
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              might be called
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} Euclidean-topological ∞-groupoids
            %p
              In fact for the discussion of just universal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
              as opposed to the higher stages in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
              it would be sufficient and more natural to take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              the full subcategory of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+simply+connected+topological+spaces"} locally simply connected topological spaces
              and consider just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
              over this site.
          %p But the following discussion is completely formal and applies globally to all such realizations. Namely all we need is that
          #AssumptionOnH.num_defn
            %h6#assumption Assumption
            %p Assume that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (n,1)-topos
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi Π
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mi Δ
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi Γ
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mo ∇
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathbf{H}
                        \\array{
                        \\overset{\Pi}{\longrightarrow}
                        \\\
                        \\overset{\Delta}{\longleftarrow}
                        \\\
                        \\overset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}
                        \\\
                        \\overset{\nabla}{\longleftarrow}
                        }
                        \\mathbf{B}
                %p
                  over the given
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (n,1)-topos
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoids"} n-groupoids
              %li
                %p
                  such that its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
                  preserves
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+products"} homotopy fiber products
                  over
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects"} discrete objects
                  (objects in the essential image of
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \&amp;#643; \coloneqq \Delta \Pi
            %p
              for the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \overset{\eta_X}{\longrightarrow} &amp;#643; X
            %p
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              morphism ona given object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Assumption
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AssumptionOnH"}
              is satisfied for the case of
              = succeed "-toposes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-cohesive+site"} ∞-cohesive site
              and for
              = succeed "-toposes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,1)
              = succeed "-cohesive" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfCohesiveToposesOfTopologicalGroupoids"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "cohesive+infinity-topos#PiPreservesPullbacksOverDiscretes"} this prop.
          %p
            Now consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
            any object, for instance a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated+object"} 0-truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+infinity-groupoid"} topological infinity-groupoid
          %p
            Assume, just for ease of discussion, that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %em geometrically connected
            in that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated+object"} 0-truncation
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape"} shape
            is
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ʃ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_0(&amp;#643; X) \simeq \ast
                  \\,.
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            in the base topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            we choose a point
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ʃ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\ast \to \tau_1(&amp;#643; X)
                  \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em universal cover
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi pb
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi τ
                                      %mn 1
                                %mo ∘
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi τ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ʃ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\hat X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;(pb)&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\underset{L_{\tau_1} \circ \eta_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \tau_1(&amp;#643; X)
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
            is immediate from the abstract setup:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
                is simply connected, in that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1 &amp;#643; \hat X \simeq \ast
              %p
                This is because
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; X
                is discrete by construction, and hence so is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ʃ
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1(&amp;#643; X)
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AssumptionOnH"}
                applying
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ʃ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643;
                to the above square yields another homotopy pullback of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi pb
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ʃ
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi τ
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;#643; \hat X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;(pb)&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;#643; X &amp;\underset{&amp;#643; \eta_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \tau_1(&amp;#643; X)
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                Now the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
                (in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
                is of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ⋯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      0 \to \pi_1(&amp;#643; \hat X) \longrightarrow \pi_1(&amp;#643; X) \overset{=}{\longrightarrow} \pi_1(\tau_1 &amp;#643; X) \to \cdots
              %p
                which implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1( &amp;#643; \hat X )
                and hence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1 &amp;#643; \hat X
                is indeed trivial.
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \longrightarrow X
                be any other object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/X}
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ʃ
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1(&amp;#643; E) \simeq \ast
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi E
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      E &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; \hat X
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; X
                      }
              %p This is because the naturality of the shape unit and of the truncation unit gives a homotopy commuting square of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi E
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi E
                            %mtd
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mi E
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi τ
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mi E
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ≃
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi τ
                                %mn 1
                              %mi ʃ
                              %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      E &amp;\overset{\eta_E}{\longrightarrow}&amp; &amp;#643; E &amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \tau_1(&amp;#643; E ) \simeq \ast
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      X &amp;\underset{\eta_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp; &amp;#643; X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \tau_1 &amp;#643; X
                      }
              %p
                and thus a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
                over the diagram which defines
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
                via its
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
          %p
            This shows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
            is the universal cover on abstract grounds.
          %p
            We may also check explicitly that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
            is given as the space of homotopy classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            from the given basepoint. To that end we use that, at least over the site
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is represented by the topological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} path ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+via+cohesive+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} shape via cohesive path ∞-groupoid
          %blockquote
            %p The following is old material that deserves to be harmonized a bit more with the above stuff.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a suitably well behaved pointed space. The universal cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is (equivalent to) the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Pi(X)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} = Sh_{(\infty,1)}(Top_{cg})
              of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} topological ∞-groupoid
            %p
              In other words, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              classified by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Pi_1(X)
              is the universal cover
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(1)}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X^{(1)} &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \Pi(X)
                    }
                    \\,.
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              \: may need polishing.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We place ourselves in the context of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} topological ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as well as its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
              and its truncation to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              as objects in there.
            %p
              The canonical morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Pi(X)
              hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Pi_1(X)
              given by the inclusion of constant paths may be regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              for a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(X)
              be the set of connected components of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "-groupoid," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(X) \to \Pi(X)
              of the projection
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X) \to \pi_0(X)
            %p
              Then the
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
              = succeed "-bundle" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Pi(X)
              is its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi UCov
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    UCov(X) &amp;\to&amp; \pi_0(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \Pi(X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              We think of this topological
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi UCov
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} UCov(X)
              as the
              %strong
                universal covering
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
              gives the ordinary universal covering space:
            %p
              for this we compute the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi UCov
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    UCov_1(X) &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{x}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \Pi_1(X)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where we assume
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to be connected with chosen baspoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              just to shorten the exposition a little. By the laws of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of a weakly equivalent diagram, where the point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              is resolved to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} universal
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X) = T_x \Pi_1(X)
                    \\,.
            %blockquote
              %p
                (More in detail, what we do behind the scenes is this: we regard the diagram as a diagram in the
                %em global
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi E
                        %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X)
                achieves. Then the ordinary pullback in the category of simplicial presheaves is the homotopy pullback in
                = succeed "-prestacks." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-stackification," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %p
              The topological groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X)
              has as objects homotopy classes rel endpoints of paths in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              starting at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and as morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo :
                    %mi γ
                    %mo →
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa : \gamma \to \gamma'
              it has commuting triangles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi γ
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; x
                    \\\
                    \&amp;{}^{\mathllap{\gamma}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\gamma'}}
                    \\\
                    y &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\kappa}{\to}&amp;&amp; y'
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi E
                              %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X) &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{x}}
                    \\\
                    \\Pi_1(X)^I &amp;\stackrel{d_0}{\to}&amp; \Pi_1(X)
                    }
            %p
              in simplicial presheaves on
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(\mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X))
              are those where the endpoint evaluation produces an open set in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p Now it is immediate to read off the homotopy pullback as the ordinary pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi UCov
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi E
                              %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    UCov_1(X) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \Pi_1(X)
                    \\,.
                    }
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is categorically discrete, this simply produces the space of objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_x \Pi_1(X)
              over the points of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              starting at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              with the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi UCov
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} UCov_1(X) \to X
              being endpoint evaluation.
            %p This indeed is then the usual construction of the universal covering space in terms of paths, as described for instance in
            %ul
              %li
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathreference.com/at-cov,build.html"} Covering spaces, Building a universal cover
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathreference.com/"} Math Reference Project
          %h3#in_the_petit_toposes_over_the_space
            In the petit
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            On the other hand, we can view a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as the little
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
            of
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is locally connected and locally simply connected in the “coverings” sense, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
            is locally 1-connected.
          %p
            In fact, for the construction of the universal cover we require only the (2,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(X)
            of sheaves (stacks) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-topos." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be any (2,1)-topos which is locally 1-connected. This means that in the unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^*,E_*)\colon E\to Gpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*
            has a left adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!\colon E \to Gpd
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+functor"} indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+of+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is defined to be
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(E)\coloneqq E_!(*)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            As discussed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+of+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} here
            in the
            = succeed "-case," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(E)
            is a left adjoint to the inclusion of groupoids into locally 1-connected (2,1)-toposes (which sends
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Gpd
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\mapsto Gpd/G \simeq Gpd^G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to \Pi_1(E)
            (where we regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(E)
            as the (2,1)-topos
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Gpd
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd^{\Pi_1(E)}
          %p
            Suppose, for simplicity, that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is connected. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(E)
            is also connected, and so we have an essentially unique functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to \Pi_1(E)
            %strong universal cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            to be the pullback (2,1)-topos:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi E
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ E^{(1)} &amp; \to &amp; E \\ \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\ * &amp; \to &amp; \Pi_1(E)}
          %p
            (where of course
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            denotes the terminal (2,1)-topos
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd
          %p
            Now observe that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to \Pi_1(E)
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+homeomorphism+of+toposes"} local homeomorphism of toposes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd \simeq Gpd/\Pi_1(E)/(*\to \Pi_1(E))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{(1)}\to E
            is also a local homeomorphism, i.e. there exists an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo ˜
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{E}\in E
            and an equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{(1)} \simeq E/\widetilde{E}
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{E}
            can be identified with the pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo ˜
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi η
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi E
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mo =
                              %msup
                                %mi E
                                %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi E
                                %mo !
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ \widetilde{E} &amp; \to &amp; * \\ \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\eta} \\ * &amp; \to &amp; E^*(\Pi_1(E)) \mathrlap{= E^*(E_!(*))}}
          %p
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to E^*(E_!(*))
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*
            applied to the unique map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to E_!(*)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!\dashv E^*
          %p
            In order to see that this is a sensible definition, we first observe that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{(1)}
            is itself locally 1-connected (since it is etale over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!(\widetilde{E}) = *
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!\dashv E^*
            (which is equivalent to saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!
            is
            = succeed "-indexed)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{E}
            implies that we also have a pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mo !
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo ˜
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mo !
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi id
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mo !
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ E_!(\widetilde{E}) &amp; \to &amp; E_!(*) \\ \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{id} \\ * &amp; \to &amp; E_!(*)}
          %p
            which clearly implies that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!(\widetilde{E}) = *
          %p
            Thus,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{(1)}
            is a connected and simply connected space with a local homeomorphism to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is locally 1-connected, as a (2,1)-category it can be generated by 1-connected objects, i.e. objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_!(U)\simeq *
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            and a
            %span.newWikiWord
              regular 1-epic
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/regular+1-epic"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to *
          %p
            We claim that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is any 1-connected object of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{E}
            is trivialized (or split) over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\times \widetilde{E}
            is equivalent, over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\times E^*S
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\in Gpd
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                          %mo ×
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo ˜
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi U
                              %mo ×
                              %mi η
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                          %mo ×
                          %msup
                            %mi E
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ U\times \widetilde{E} &amp; \to &amp; U \\ \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{U\times \eta} \\ U &amp; \to &amp; U\times E^*(\Pi_1(E)).}
          %p
            But
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\times E^*(\Pi_1(E)) \cong (E/U)^* (\Pi_1(E))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi U
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to (E/U)^* (\Pi_1(E))
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the same as to give a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E/U)_!(*) \to \Pi_1(E)
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
